# nodus/oevm/tests/target/liveness-noradio.env — rete#274's regression gate
#
# THE ABSENCE OF CONF_EXTRA IS THE SUBJECT OF THIS ROW, NOT AN OMISSION FROM IT.
# Read that twice before "fixing" this file, because adding the radio back is the one
# edit that silently turns it into a duplicate of liveness-heartbeat and deletes the
# only gate rete#274 has. Its sibling's header argues at length that TimerlessNodeC6
# CANNOT run without a radio; that was true when it was written and rete#274 is what
# changed it. The two rows now differ by exactly one variable, and that variable is
# the whole test.
#
# WHAT WENT WRONG (rete#274, H6 of the 2026-08-27 liveness review). The base tick is
# registered by the BRIDGE — `PortaBridge>>startTickingOn:` since rete#440 R2 — and the bridge used to be
# constructed inside the `ifFalse:` branch of the socket bind. `prj.conf` carries
# NETWORKING/IPV6/UDP/SOCKETS but no L2, so a C6 built without the OpenThread overlay has
# no interface, `net udpBindPort:` answers nil, and the bridge was never built. No bridge
# meant no `startTicking:`, which was the ONLY timer registration in this image: the node
# ticked nothing, wedged never, and put no deadline in `timer_target_snapshot`.
# `observer_core_verdict()` answers OBS_COND_NONE at n == 0, and OBS_COND_NONE is
# indistinguishable from health — so the node was not judged well, it was UNJUDGEABLE,
# and nothing said so. `pulse_pump` blocks on K_FOREVER whether idle or wedged, so the
# console could not tell them apart either.
#
# Not hypothetical, and it cost a board cycle to read: 2026-08-22 10:49 this node was
# built with no radio layer and sat in total silence for the full 300 s.
#
# WHAT THIS ROW WITNESSES. The bridge is now constructed with whatever `udpBindPort:`
# answered — a socket or nil — and `liveness:` + `startTickingOn:` run unconditionally, so
# a radio-less node ticks, wedges and carries a deadline exactly as a bridged one does.
# It simply reports to nobody. The PASS is therefore the ORDINARY liveness-heartbeat
# story told under the condition that used to produce nothing at all:
#
#   1. `timerless: bind FAILED — still ticking and still judgeable, but reporting to
#      nobody` on the console. This line is EXPECTED here and is not a failure.
#   2. `timerless tick N` climbing at 2 s. Before rete#274 there were none.
#   3. the wedge at tick 15, the detector firing on deadline=16000ms (cadence 2000 x
#      slack 8, still the only timer in the image), a reboot, and boot 2 reporting
#      `pass=2 fail=0`.
#
# THE FAILURE THIS GATE IS SHAPED TO CATCH is silence — the same silence as 2026-08-22.
# A regression here does not produce a wrong answer, it produces NO answer, which is why
# the row is worth its five minutes: the defect's whole character was that it was
# invisible from every side. TIMEOUT with no TAP is the red, and it is a real red.
#
# WHAT THIS ROW CANNOT SEE. Everything liveness-heartbeat's header disclaims, plus one
# of its own: with no radio there is no porta, so `sys/panic` delivery is NOT exercised
# here. That is liveness-heartbeat's job and rete#114's row in porta_sync. This row is
# about whether a deadline EXISTS, not about whether anyone hears the result.
#
# WHY IT DOES NOT SHARE liveness-heartbeat's MANIFEST. The two scenarios differ only in
# build configuration, and an .nsl file cannot see Kconfig, so the workload cannot name
# which one it is running as — hence TAP_NAME below, exactly as WedgeProbeC6 serves both
# wedge-note and wedge-detect. deploy_flash.sh's rete#215 guard covers the hazard that
# creates: a manifest that wants no overlay run after one that did forces --pristine, so
# this row cannot inherit the radio from its sibling's warm build dir and score a green
# against a build that had an interface after all.
#
# Timing is liveness-heartbeat's, unchanged: 15 ticks x 2 s to the wedge, 16 s of budget,
# up to 1 s of observer tick, a cold reboot and boot 2's first tick — ~55 s observed, 300 s
# the outer bound. OBSERVE_S outlasts the verdict on purpose (rete#216).
#
# class=disruptive: it wedges and reboots the board on purpose. A disposable board only.
SCENARIO=liveness-noradio
TAP_NAME=timerless
NODE=TimerlessNodeC6.nsl
BOARD_ID=esp32c6
CLASS=disruptive
TIMEOUT_S=300

OBSERVE_S=180
OBSERVE_PROGRESS='^.*timerless tick [0-9]+'
